voids all traffic collapsing onto slot 0.\n- Keep single selection call, no loops: Only one bpf_sk_select_reuseport call; no retries.\n- Fast mapping to range: Power-of-two masking fast path; otherwise use 64-bit multiply-high to avoid division.\n\nVerifier/Perf:\n- No unbounded loops, fixed stack, allowed helpers only (bpf_get_smp_processor_id, map lookup, select).\n- Minimal extra instructions with meaningful distribution benefits, expected to flatten p99 and reduce variance at higher rates.\n*/\n //go:build ignore\n\n#include <linux/bpf.h>\n#include <bpf/bpf_helpers.h>\n\nstruct {\n    __uint(type, BPF_MAP_TYPE_REUSEPORT_SOCKARRAY);\n    __uint(max_entries, 128);\n    __type(key, __u32);\n    __type(value, __u32);\n    __uint(pinning, LIBBPF_PIN_BY_NAME);\n} pebble_udp_targets SEC(\".maps\");\n\nstruct agent_state {\n    __u32 active;\n    __u32 pad;\n};\n\nstruct {\n    __uint(type, BPF_MAP_TYPE_ARRAY);\n    __uint(max_entries, 1);\n    __type(key, __u32);\n    __type(value, struct agent_state);\n    __uint(pinning, LIBBPF_PIN_BY_NAME);\n} pebble_agent_state SEC(\".maps\");\n\n // EVOLVE-BLOCK-START\nSEC(\"sk_reuseport/selector\")\nenum sk_action agent_udp_selector(struct sk_reuseport_md *reuse)\n{\n    __u32 key = 0;\n    struct agent_state *state = bpf_map_lookup_elem(&pebble_agent_state, &key);\n    __u32 active = state ? state->active : 0;\n\n    if (active == 0)\n        return SK_PASS;\n\n    if (active > 128)\n        active = 128;\n\n    /* If only one socket is active, avoid extra work. */\n    if (active == 1) {\n        __u32 slot0 = 0;\n        bpf_sk_select_reuseport(reuse, &pebble_udp_targets, &slot0, 0);\n        return SK_PASS;\n    }\n\n    __u32 h = reuse->hash;\n\n    /* If kernel didn't provide a useful hash, synthesize a simple one. */\n    if (h == 0) {\n        h = (__u32)reuse->len ^ ((__u32)reuse->ip_protocol << 16) ^ 0x9e3779b9;\n    }\n\n    /* Rotate mapping per-CPU to reduce cross-CPU contention hot-spots. */\n    __u32 cpu = (__u32)bpf_get_smp_processor_id();\n    h ^= cpu * 0x9e3779b1u;\n\n    __u32 slot;\n    if ((active & (active - 1)) == 0) {\n        /* Power-of-two fanout: use bitmask for minimal overhead */\n        slot = h & (active - 1);\n    } else {\n        /* Division-free mapping: slot = floor((h * active) / 2^32) */\n        __u64 prod = (__u64)h * (__u64)active;\n        slot = (__u32)(prod >> 32);\n    }\n\n    /* Single call to select; kernel only considers one call anyway */\n    bpf_sk_select_reuseport(reuse, &pebble_udp_targets, &slot, 0);\n    return SK_PASS;\n}\n // EVOLVE-BLOCK-END\n\nchar _license[] SEC(\"license\") = \"GPL\";\n", "metrics": {"policy": "agent", "rates": [40000, 60000], "load_p99_curve": [[40000.0, 2.321], [60000.0, 2.882]], "load_p99_stddev_curve": [[40000.0, 0.0], [60000.0, 0.0]], "compile": 1.0, "load": 1.0, "combined_score": -5.203, "run_success": 1.0}, "log_metric": [], "parent_program": {"id": "0675d1a1-9ae2-4061-940f-4fd59b2884f8", "code": "/*\nApproach and rationale:\n\nThis selector targets lower per-packet CPU cost and flatter tail latency by:\n- Eliminating the retry loop: We only invoke bpf_sk_select_reuseport once. The kernel considers at most one call anyway, so looping only burns cycles and adds tail latency under load.\n- Using division-free slot mapping: We map the kernel-provided hash to [0, active) with a 64-bit multiply-high reduction (slot = (hash * active) >> 32). This avoids variable division, which is expensive in eBPF, while preserving uniformity if the hash is uniform.\n- Clamping and safety: We clamp the \"active\" sockets to the map's max (128) and return SK_PASS if inactive to stay robust.\n- Fast-path for power-of-two fanout: If active is a power of two, we use a bitmask instead of the multiply-high method. This is even cheaper and common in high-performance hashing.\n- Deterministic, verifier-friendly code: No unbounded loops, one helper call, fixed stack usage, and only data from sk_reuseport_md is used, satisfying verifier constraints.\n\nExpected impact:\n- Lower per-packet instruction count and helper overhead compared to the previous rotating retry loop, reducing median and tail latency at higher request rates.\n- Stable distribution across sockets thanks to hash-to-range mapping that avoids modulo, improving throughput without adding jitter.\n*/\n //go:build ignore\n\n#include <linux/bpf.h>\n#include <bpf/bpf_helpers.h>\n\nstruct {\n    __uint(type, BPF_MAP_TYPE_REUSEPORT_SOCKARRAY);\n    __uint(max_entries, 128);\n    __type(key, __u32);\n    __type(value, __u32);\n    __uint(pinning, LIBBPF_PIN_BY_NAME);\n} pebble_udp_targets SEC(\".maps\");\n\nstruct agent_state {\n    __u32 active;\n    __u32 pad;\n};\n\nstruct {\n    __uint(type, BPF_MAP_TYPE_ARRAY);\n    __uint(max_entries, 1);\n    __type(key, __u32);\n    __type(value, struct agent_state);\n    __uint(pinning, LIBBPF_PIN_BY_NAME);\n} pebble_agent_state SEC(\".maps\");\n\n // EVOLVE-BLOCK-START\n\nSEC(\"sk_reuseport/selector\")\nenum sk_action agent_udp_selector(struct sk_reuseport_md *reuse)\n{\n    __u32 key = 0;\n    struct agent_state *state = bpf_map_lookup_elem(&pebble_agent_state, &key);\n    __u32 active = state ? state->active : 0;\n\n    if (active == 0)\n        return SK_PASS;\n\n    if (active > 128)\n        active = 128;\n\n    __u32 h = reuse->hash;\n    __u32 slot;\n\n    if ((active & (active - 1)) == 0) {\n        /* Power-of-two fanout: use bitmask for minimal overhead */\n        slot = h & (active - 1);\n    } else {\n        /* Division-free mapping: slot = floor((h * active) / 2^32) */\n        __u64 prod = (__u64)h * (__u64)active;\n        slot = (__u32)(prod >> 32);\n    }\n\n    /* Single call to select; kernel only considers one call anyway */\n    bpf_sk_select_reuseport(reuse, &pebble_udp_targets, &slot, 0);\n    return SK_PASS;\n}\n // EVOLVE-BLOCK-END\n\nchar _license[] SEC(\"license\") = \"GPL\";\n", "language": "cpp", "parent_id": null, "generation": 0, "timestamp": 1763044159.5422359, "iteration_found": 0, "metrics": {"policy": "agent", "rates": [40000, 60000], "load_p99_curve": [[40000.0, 2.497], [60000.0, 4.822]], "load_p99_stddev_curve": [[40000.0, 0.0], [60000.0, 0.0]], "compile": 1.0, "load": 1.0, "combined_score": -7.319, "run_success": 1.0}, "complexity": 0.0, "diversity": 0.0, "metadata": {"island": 0}, "prompts": null, "artifacts_json": null, "artifact_dir": null, "embedding": null}, "parent_metrics": {"policy": "agent", "rates": [40000, 60000], "load_p99_curve": [[40000.0, 2.497], [60000.0, 4.822]], "load_p99_stddev_curve": [[40000.0, 0.0], [60000.0, 0.0]], "compile": 1.0, "load": 1.0, "combined_score": -7.319, "run_success": 1.0}, "parent_perf_expl": null, "code_summary": "{\n  \"overview\": {\n    \"scope\": \"Synthetic UDP storage emulator with eBPF-aware load balancing (pebble-server) — only internal/, cmd/, scripts/, workload/, run.sh, run_exp.py included.\",\n    \"languages\": [\n      \"Go 1.22 (internal/*, cmd/*)\",\n      \"Bash (run.sh, scripts/*, workload/run_client.sh)\",\n      \"Python 3 (run_exp.py, scripts/dispatch_docker_experiments.py)\"\n    ],\n    \"artifact_conventions\": {\n      \"logs\": \"logs/<role> (server|client)\",\n      \"results\": \"results/run-* (per run.sh invocation) containing experiment.json + workload_summary.json\",\n      \"eBPF_pin_paths\": \"/sys/fs/bpf/pebble/<RUN_ID> (set by run.sh before launching the Go server)\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"execution_flow\": [\n    {\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"name\": \"Experiment orchestration\",\n      \"artefact\": \"run_exp.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Thin experiment wrapper: either shells into run.sh for fresh sweeps or parses dispatch manifests to summarise existing runs, then emits summary.json and optional matplotlib plots.\",\n      \"key_steps\": [\n        \"parse_args (run_exp.py:29-95) exposes policies/rates/threads plus manifest + plotting toggles.\",\n        \"invoke_run_sh/load_manifest_runs gather `run-*` directories, extract metrics from workload_summary.json, and pass records into write_experiment_summary/generate_plots.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 2,\n      \"name\": \"Per-run workflow\",\n      \"artefact\": \"run.sh\",\n      \"description\": \"Convenience script that (a) slices NUMA CPUs between server/client, (b) rebuilds eBPF assets, (c) restarts the Go server for each workload iteration, (d) runs cmd/workload_client under taskset, and (e) aggregates iteration outputs into workload_summary.json.\",\n      \"key_steps\": [\n        \"resolve_cpu_pool/join_by (run.sh:27-118) derive SERVER_CPUSET + CLIENT_CPUSET from CPUSET_POOL or NUMA node 0.\",\n        \"Calls scripts/build_ebpf.sh + scripts/cleanup_ebpf_maps.sh, then orchestrates server via scripts/launch_server.sh and client via run_client wrapper.\",\n        \"Embedded Python (run.sh:415-452) regex-parses client logs into workload_summary.json; final line prints the run directory for downstream tooling.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 3,\n      \"name\": \"Runtime services\",\n      \"artefacts\": [\n        \"cmd/pebble_server/main.go:21-91 -> internal/server/*\",\n        \"cmd/workload_client/main.go:67-450\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Go binaries that run.sh controls. The server exposes UDP reuseport workers with synthetic latency and optional eBPF selection, while the workload client generates GET/SCAN traffic with latency tracking.\",\n      \"key_steps\": [\n        \"cmd/pebble_server wires CLI flags, creates log/results dirs, enables pprof/profiling, builds server.Config and runs server.New/Run under signal-aware context.\",\n        \"internal/server.Server.New/Run (server.go:104-181) validate config, load eBPF policy, clear pinned maps, then open reuseport sockets, attach eBPF, and spawn workers; handleRequest (server.go:268-325) executes busy-wait delays and records stats.\",\n        \"cmd/workload_client main loop (main.go:67-347) builds UDP payloads, enforces rate limit via golang.org/x