nt.c:57-86). When the chosen worker is momentarily full, the kernel falls back to its default reuseport hash instead of probing other sockets, so bursts pile onto whichever worker the fallback prefers, stretching per-request wait time even at moderate load.  \\n- At 80\\u202fk rps the p99 drops slightly (10.7\\u202fms vs 12.6\\u202fms baseline) because the loop-free arithmetic reduces per-packet instruction count compared to the 128-iteration probe loop in the prior version (ebpf/agent_backup.c:37-50), trimming CPU cycles when queues are mostly empty.  \\n- 100\\u202fk rps p99 exploded from 0.86\\u202fs to 4.47\\u202fs. Under this load, workers frequently reject the first slot (EBUSY). The previous program kept probing until it found a socket whose backlog could absorb the packet, keeping queues balanced; the new one immediately defers to kernel fallback, so the same hot socket sees repeated retries and multi-second queues.  \\n- 140\\u202fk rps improves vs baseline (3.86\\u202fs vs 6.59\\u202fs) because the old loop burned so much time per packet that even successful reroutes still paid the instruction tax, whereas the streamlined math keeps CPU overhead lower once all workers are saturated. Tail latency is still seconds because packets queue behind long SCAN handlers once the socket selection stops skipping congested workers.\\n\\n**Did the behavior achieve the program\\u2019s intent?**  \\nIntent: deterministically hash each packet into the active worker set while avoiding the costly probe loop (ebpf/agent.c:57-86 comments). The behavior partially failed: it delivered better top-end throughput efficiency (seen at 140\\u202fk), but it no longer enforces \\u201cfind an available worker\\u201d fairness once a slot is backlogged, so p99 collapsed at 100\\u202fk despite the same worker count. Success: lower instruction cost at highest load. Failure: fairness/congestion-avoidance goal wasn\\u2019t met because single-attempt routing created persistent hotspot queues (100\\u202fk regression).\\n\\n**Missing signals & new metrics/logs to add**  \\n- **Per-worker `bpf_sk_select_reuseport` success/fail counters**: instrument the userspace agent state map or server logs to count helper return codes per worker; shows whether single-attempt routing is hitting busy sockets.  \\n- **Per-socket queue depth / outstanding requests**: have each worker export backlog length or time-in-queue every second from `internal/server/server.go`; would confirm whether one worker is overloaded when tails spike at 100\\u202fk.\"}", "artifact_dir": "/home/benny/evolve_agent/agentic-ebpf/pebble-server/openevolve_output/db/artifacts/4f939d7d-9185-4069-9da0-75c8f987f576", "embedding": null}, "parent_metrics": {"policy": "agent", "rates": [50000, 60000, 80000, 100000, 140000], "load_p99_curve": [[50000.0, 5.839], [60000.0, 23.415], [80000.0, 10.745], [100000.0, 4465.972], [140000.0, 3864.677]], "load_p99_stddev_curve": [[50000.0, 0.0], [60000.0, 0.0], [80000.0, 0.0], [100000.0, 0.0], [140000.0, 0.0]], "compile": 1.0, "load": 1.0, "combined_score": -21186.802, "run_success": 1.0}, "parent_perf_expl": "**Behavior & Performance (Medium)**  \n- 50–80 k rps stayed in the single-digit ms range but regressed vs the baseline at 50/60 k (5.8 ms vs 3.6 ms, 23 ms vs 17 ms) because the new selector always makes exactly one `bpf_sk_select_reuseport` attempt and unconditionally returns `SK_PASS` regardless of helper failure (ebpf/agent.c:57-86). When the chosen worker is momentarily full, the kernel falls back to its default reuseport hash instead of probing other sockets, so bursts pile onto whichever worker the fallback prefers, stretching per-request wait time even at moderate load.  \n- At 80 k rps the p99 drops slightly (10.7 ms vs 12.6 ms baseline) because the loop-free arithmetic reduces per-packet instruction count compared to the 128-iteration probe loop in the prior version (ebpf/agent_backup.c:37-50), trimming CPU cycles when queues are mostly empty.  \n- 100 k rps p99 exploded from 0.86 s to 4.47 s. Under this load, workers frequently reject the first slot (EBUSY). The previous program kept probing until it found a socket whose backlog could absorb the packet, keeping queues balanced; the new one immediately defers to kernel fallback, so the same hot socket sees repeated retries and multi-second queues.  \n- 140 k rps improves vs baseline (3.86 s vs 6.59 s) because the old loop burned so much time per packet that even successful reroutes still paid the instruction tax, whereas the streamlined math keeps CPU overhead lower once all workers are saturated. Tail latency is still seconds because packets queue behind long SCAN handlers once the socket selection stops skipping congested workers.\n\n**Did the behavior achieve the program’s intent?**  \nIntent: deterministically hash each packet into the active worker set while avoiding the costly probe loop (ebpf/agent.c:57-86 comments). The behavior partially failed: it delivered better top-end throughput efficiency (seen at 140 k), but it no longer enforces “find an available worker” fairness once a slot is backlogged, so p99 collapsed at 100 k despite the same worker count. Success: lower instruction cost at highest load. Failure: fairness/congestion-avoidance goal wasn’t met because single-attempt routing created persistent hotspot queues (100 k regression).\n\n**Missing signals & new metrics/logs to add**  \n- **Per-worker `bpf_sk_select_reuseport` success/fail counters**: instrument the userspace agent state map or server logs to count helper return codes per worker; shows whether single-attempt routing is hitting busy sockets.  \n- **Per-socket queue depth / outstanding requests**: have each worker export backlog length or time-in-queue every second from `internal/server/server.go`; would confirm whether one worker is overloaded when tails spike at 100 k.", "code_summary": "{\n  \"overview\": {\n    \"scope\": \"Synthetic UDP storage emulator with eBPF-aware load balancing (pebble-server) — only internal/, cmd/, scripts/, workload/, run.sh, run_exp.py included.\",\n    \"languages\": [\n      \"Go 1.22 (internal/*, cmd/*)\",\n      \"Bash (run.sh, scripts/*, workload/run_client.sh)\",\n      \"Python 3 (run_exp.py, scripts/dispatch_docker_experiments.py)\"\n    ],\n    \"artifact_conventions\": {\n      \"logs\": \"logs/<role> (server|client)\",\n      \"results\": \"results/run-* (per run.sh invocation) containing experiment.json + workload_summary.json\",\n      \"eBPF_pin_paths\": \"/sys/fs/bpf/pebble/<RUN_ID> (set by run.sh before launching the Go server)\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"execution_flow\": [\n    {\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"name\": \"Experiment orchestration\",\n      \"artefact\": \"run_exp.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Thin experiment wrapper: either shells into run.sh for fresh sweeps or parses dispatch manifests to summarise existing runs, then emits summary.json and optional matplotlib plots.\",\n      \"key_steps\": [\n        \"parse_args (run_exp.py:29-95) exposes policies/rates/threads plus manifest + plotting toggles.\",\n        \"invoke_run_sh/load_manifest_runs gather `run-*` directories, extract metrics from workload_summary.json, and pass records into write_experiment_summary/generate_plots.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 2,\n      \"name\": \"Per-run workflow\",\n      \"artefact\": \"run.sh\",\n      \"description\": \"Convenience script that (a) slices NUMA CPUs between server/client, (b) rebuilds eBPF assets, (c) restarts the Go server for each workload iteration, (d) runs cmd/workload_client under taskset, and (e) aggregates iteration outputs into workload_summary.json.\",\n      \"key_steps\": [\n        \"resolve_cpu_pool/join_by (run.sh:27-118) derive SERVER_CPUSET + CLIENT_CPUSET from CPUSET_POOL or NUMA node 0.\",\n        \"Calls scripts/build_ebpf.sh + scripts/cleanup_ebpf_maps.sh, then orchestrates server via scripts/launch_server.sh and client via run_client wrapper.\",\n        \"Embedded Python (run.sh:415-452) regex-parses client logs into workload_summary.json; final line prints the run directory for downstream tooling.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 3,\n      \"name\": \"Runtime services\",\n      \"artefacts\": [\n        \"cmd/pebble_server/main.go:21-91 -> internal/server/*\",\n        \"cmd/workload_client/main.go:67-450\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Go binaries that run.sh controls. The server exposes UDP reuseport workers with synthetic latency and optional eBPF selection, while the workload client generates GET/SCAN traffic with latency tracking.\",\n      \"key_steps\": [\n        \"cmd/pebble_server wires CLI flags, creates log/results dirs, enables pprof/profiling, builds server.Config and runs server.New/Run under signal-aware context.\",\n        \"internal/server.Server.New/Run (server.go:104-181) validate config, load eBPF policy, clear pinned maps, then open reuseport sockets, attach eBPF, and spawn workers; handleRequest (server.go:268-325) executes busy-wait delays and records stats.\",\n        \"cmd/workload_client main loop (main.go:67-347) builds UDP payloads, enforces rate limit via golang.org/x/time/rate, tags each request with reqID (makeReqID/parseReqID, main.go:308-337) so receive goroutines can compute latency and feed the aggregator (latencyAggregator, main.go:40-66).\",\n        \"Server stats logger (server.go:328-395) emits per-worker and aggregate lines that scripts/monitoring can scrape.\"\n      ],\n      \"downstream\": [\n        \"Server relies on internal/server/ebpf.go + generated internal/ebpfutil bindings.\",\n        \"Client output is parsed by run.sh’s Python aggregator; logs feed human debugging.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 4,\n      \"name\": \"Support scripts\",\n      \"artefacts\": [\n        \"scripts/build_ebpf.sh:1-34\",\n        \"scripts/cleanup_ebpf_maps.sh:1-25\",\n        \"scripts/launch_server.sh:1-96\",\n        \"scripts/dispatch_docker_experiments.py:1-654\",\n        \"workload/run_client.sh:1-62\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Reusable helpers for building eBPF assets, cleaning pinned maps, launching the server standalone, dispatching dockerized experiments, and invoking the workload client without run.sh.\",\n      \"key_steps\": [\n        \"build_ebpf.sh enforces clang availability, sets BPF_CLANG/BPF_CFLAGS, adds arch include paths, then runs `go generate ./internal/ebpfutil`.\",\n        \"cleanup_ebpf_maps.sh deletes global pinned maps unless run-specific BPF_PIN_PATH is set, preventing fd leaks between runs.\",\n        \"launch_server.sh builds cmd/pebble_server (unless disabled), enforces single instance via PID file, applies taskset when SERVER_CPUSET is exported, and records PID for run.sh.\",\n        \"dispatch_docker_experiments.py reads NUMA topology (read_numa_cpu_map, line 106), assigns per-container CPU slices, constructs docker run commands (build_jobs, line 149), streams logs asynchronously (run_job, line 221), and optionally post-processes with run_exp.py.\",\n        \"workload/run_client.sh is a thin CLI around `go run ./cmd/workload_client` for ad-hoc manual traffic.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"modules\": {\n    \"run_exp.py\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Top-level wrapper to sweep policies/rates and collect workload_summary.json files into one experiment summary.\",\n      \"key_points\": [\n        \"parse_args exposes knobs for policies/rates, send-workers, duration, server/client cores, plotting, and manifest reuse.\",\n        \"invoke_run_sh executes run.sh and captures the run directory; load_manifest_runs + link_run_directories reuse docker-dispatched runs.\",\n        \"generate_overall_plot / generate_get_scan_plot optionally render PNGs (skip with --skip-plot).\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"run.sh\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Automation glue that sets up CPU pinning, rebuilds eBPF assets, runs cmd/pebble_server + cmd/workload_client for N iterations, and emits workload_summary.json.\",\n      \"key_points\": [\n        \"resolve_cpu_pool + join_by compute SERVER_CPUSET/CLIENT_CPUSET and export them for both taskset prefixes.\",\n        \"start_server/stop_server wrap scripts/launch_server.sh and enforce clean PID files; run_client pins workload_client under CLIENT_CPUSET.\",\n        \"Embedded Python generates workload_summary.json from logs/workload_iteration_*.txt, which run_exp.py later ingests.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"cmd/pebble_server\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Go binary that instantiates internal/server.Server based on CLI flags and keeps it running with profiling enabled.\",\n      \"key_sections\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Flag wiring & filesystem setup\",\n          \"lines\": \"cmd/pebble_server/main.go:21-52\",\n          \"details\": [\n            \"Defines flags for listen addr, workers, policy, max scan, log/results dirs, timeouts, and synthetic delays; ensures directories exist before logging.\",\n            \"Creates/opens <log-dir>/server.log (append mode) and builds a microsecond-resolution logger.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Profiling + server lifecycle\",\n          \"lines\": \"cmd/pebble_server/main.go:52-92\",\n          \"details\": [\n            \"Enables block/mutex profiling (runtime.SetBlockProfileRate/SetMutexProfileFraction) and hosts net/http/pprof on 127.0.0.1:6060.\",\n            \"Builds server.Config, calls server.New (fails fast on invalid config or eBPF load issues), installs SIGINT/SIGTERM handler, logs startup configuration, and blocks on srv.Run(ctx).\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"cross_dependencies\": [\n        \"Uses internal/server (Config, Server, eBPF loader).\",\n        \"scripts/launch_server.sh expects -log-dir and -results-dir to exist for log collation.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"cmd/workload_client\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Open-loop UDP workload generator with reqID-based latency measurement and throughput reporting.\",\n      \"key_sections\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Latency data structures\",\n          \"lines\": \"cmd/workload_client/main.go:32-66\",\n          \"details\": [\n            \"latencyRecord and latencyAggregator store per-request latencies, split into overall/GET/SCAN slices; aggregator.totalRecv reports sample counts.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Main workload loop\",\n          \"lines\": \"cmd/workload_client/main.go:67-307\",\n          \"details\": [\n            \"Parses flags (server, duration, rate, get-frac, scan-limit, key prefix/space, log path, send workers), validates arguments, seeds RNGs per worker.\",\n            \"Creates a shared rate limiter (golang.org/x/time/rate), spawns send goroutines that build payloads (buildPayload, line 363) and assign reqIDs (makeReqID, line 308).\",\n            \"Spawns recv goroutines with deadlines that parse responses, extract reqIDs (parseReqID, line 320), compute latency, and push records into latencyCh.\",\n            \"Aggregator + monitor goroutines track outstanding requests and total received counts.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"Statistics reporting\",\n          \"lines\": \"cmd/workload_client/main.go:308-451\",\n          \"details\": [\n            \"Helper functions (makeReqID/parseReqID/writeHex/parseHex) ensure both sides share the encoding.\",\n            \"percentile/average/reportLatencyStats (lines 376-451) sort copies of the latency slices, compute p50/p90/p99/avg, and print textual summaries that run.sh’s regex parser expects.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"cross_dependencies\": [\n        \"run.sh’s run_client wrapper invokes this with -log pointing at logs/client.log; workload/run_client.sh uses go run for convenience.\",\n        \"Server assumes GET payload format 'GET key [reqID]' and SCAN 'SCAN start limit [reqID]' as implemented here.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"internal/server\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Core server runtime, including configuration validation, UDP worker pool, request parser, stats logging, and eBPF policy integration.\",\n      \"key_files\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"internal/server/config.go\",\n          \"summary\": \"Config struct + Validate clamp runtime knobs to sane defaults so CLI/script errors don’t crash the server.\",\n          \"key_functions\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"Config.Validate\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/config.go:19-43\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Sets ListenAddr default (127.0.0.1:9000), ensures at least one worker, caps MaxScanKeys >= 1 (default 100k), enforces non-zero timeouts/delays.\",\n                \"Called by server.New before any socket/eBPF work, giving run.sh freedom to pass zero/negative placeholder values.\"\n              ]\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"internal/server/server.go\",\n          \"summary\": \"Implements the Server struct, worker lifecycle, UDP handler, and stats reporter.\",\n          \"key_functions\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"Server.New\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/server.go:104-131\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Validates config, builds default logger when nil, loads eBPF policy via loadEBPF, clears pinned target map when a program is present, and preallocates workerStats.\"\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"Server.Run\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/server.go:144-182\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Resets stats, spawns stats logger, iterates workers to open UDP sockets (openWorker, lines 184-230), optionally attaches the eBPF program to worker 0, records socket fds into the pinned map, launches spawnWorker goroutines, and blocks until ctx cancellation.\"\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"openWorker + spawnWorker\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/server.go:184-266\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"openWorker sets SO_REUSEADDR/SO_REUSEPORT via net.ListenConfig.Control and attaches the eBPF program once; returns both UDPConn and fd for map updates.\",\n                \"spawnWorker loops on ReadFromUDP, handles ctx cancellation/ErrClosed gracefully, and logs transient read/write errors.\"\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"handleRequest\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/server.go:268-325\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Parses payloads via parseRequest, extracts optional reqID tokens, enforces SCAN limit <= MaxScanKeys, executes accurate busy-wait delays for GET/SCAN, records latencies per worker, and formats responses (formatResponse, lines 397-407).\"\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"startStatsLogger\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/server.go:328-395\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Every second, snapshots worker metrics, logs per-worker averages when there was traffic, accumulates totals, and emits aggregate '[perf] interval=1s ...' lines consumed by observability tooling.\"\n              ]\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"internal/server/handler.go\",\n          \"summary\": \"Robust ASCII parser for GET/SCAN requests.\",\n          \"key_functions\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"parseRequest\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/handler.go:14-45\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Trims whitespace, splits fields, enforces argument counts for GET/SCAN, and lowercases manually via equalFoldASCII (lines 48-66) to avoid allocations in hot paths.\"\n              ]\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"internal/server/ebpf.go\",\n          \"summary\": \"Loads eBPF selector programs, manages pin directories, and updates reuseport target maps.\",\n          \"key_functions\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"loadEBPF + load* variants\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/ebpf.go:50-218\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"Switches on policy names, ensures memlock rlimit is raised, creates pin directories, loads generated ebpfutil objects, seeds state maps (e.g., PebbleRrState.Active = workers), and returns ebpfPolicy handles with Close hooks.\",\n                \"Validates non-negative worker counts for agent/scan_split/hash policies.\"\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"attach/updateTargetsMap/clearTargets\",\n              \"lines\": \"internal/server/ebpf.go:220-268\",\n              \"details\": [\n                \"attach(fd) wraps SO_ATTACH_REUSEPORT_EBPF, updateTargetsMap writes worker fd values into the pinned pebble_udp_targets map so eBPF programs can redirect flows, clearTargets removes stale slots at startup (skips when map not present).\"\n              ]\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"cross_dependencies\": [\n        \"Relies on generated internal/ebpfutil bindings (bpf2go outputs).\",\n        \"Server expects run.sh or scripts/launch_server.sh to set BPF_PIN_BASE/PATH correctly.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"internal/ebpfutil\": {\n      \"high_level_role\": \"Generated Go bindings/objects for each eBPF selector program; rebuild with `go generate ./internal/ebpfutil`.\",\n      \"key_files\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"internal/ebpfutil/bpf_assets.go\",\n          \"summary\": \"Contains go:generate directives pointing at ../../ebpf/*.c programs with bpf2go, ensuring clang builds BPF object files.\",\n          \"key_points\": [\n            \"Generated *_bpf.go files (e.g., agentselector_bpf.go) expose typed structs (AgentSelectorObjects, Maps, Programs) and embed corresponding *.o bytecode, which internal/server/ebpf.go loads with pinned map support.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"cross_dependencies\": [\n        \"scripts/build_ebpf.sh must run before any policy other than 'default' is used, otherwise loadEBPF will fail due to missing object files.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"scripts\": {\n      \"build_ebpf.sh\": {\n        \"role\": \"Rebuild internal/ebpfutil assets (`go generate ./internal/ebpfutil`) with clang, unless SKIP_EBPF_BUILD=true.\"\n      },\n      \"cleanup_ebpf_maps.sh\": {\n        \"role\": \"Remove pinned reuseport maps under $BPF_PIN_BASE to avoid stale file descriptor slots; skipped when BPF_PIN_PATH is set.\"\n      },\n      \"launch_server.sh\": {\n        \"role\": \"Build/run cmd/pebble_server with provided flags, enforce single instance via PID files, and optionally wrap in taskset.\"\n      },\n      \"dispatch_docker_experiments.py\": {\n        \"role\": \"NUMA-aware docker dispatcher: builds `docker run` commands per (policy, rate), streams logs, writes dispatch manifests, and can trigger run_exp.py on completion.\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"workload\": {\n      \"run_client.sh\": {\n        \"role\": \"Simplified wrapper to run cmd/workload_client without building binaries.\",\n        \"lines\": \"workload/run_client.sh:1-62\",\n        \"notes\": [\n          \"Accepts basic knobs (-s server, -t duration, -r rate, -g GET fraction, -m scan limit, -k prefix, -N key space, -w workers, -l log file).\",\n          \"Ensures client log directory exists, runs from repo root so go modules resolve, and writes logs to logs/client.log by default.\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n"}
